Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• DICOM_PIVOT."collection_id": filter rows that belong to the “qin_prostate_repeatability” collection.  
• DICOM_PIVOT."SeriesDescription": locate series that contain text such as “DWI”, “T2 Weighted Axial”, or “Apparent Diffusion Coefficient”.  
• DICOM_PIVOT."StudyInstanceUID": the study identifier we must count uniquely.  
• DICOM_PIVOT."SeriesInstanceUID": primary key for an imaging series; needed to link to segmentation rows.  
• SEGMENTATIONS."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID": SeriesInstanceUID of the source (“segmented”) image series; lets us connect a segmentation object back to its parent T2 Weighted Axial series.  
• SEGMENTATIONS."StudyInstanceUID": study identifier found on the SEGMENT object itself (can confirm linkage).  

Typical conditions that may be useful  
• "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'  
• "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%'  
• "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'  
• "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'  

Below are ten progressively more‑complex Snowflake SQL queries (all limited to 20 rows where appropriate) that can be executed to explore the data and derive the final count of unique StudyInstanceUIDs.  
Each query is preceded by a brief description.

```sql
-- 1. List 20 rows from the collection to verify the basic fields.
SELECT
  "StudyInstanceUID",
  "SeriesInstanceUID",
  "SeriesDescription"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Inspect distinct SeriesDescription values in the collection.
SELECT DISTINCT
  "SeriesDescription"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Count unique StudyInstanceUIDs that have a DWI series.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID") AS "dwi_study_count"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%';
```

```sql
-- 4. Count unique StudyInstanceUIDs that have a T2 Weighted Axial series.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID") AS "t2_axial_study_count"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%';
```

```sql
-- 5. Count unique StudyInstanceUIDs that have an Apparent Diffusion Coefficient series.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID") AS "adc_study_count"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%';
```

```sql
-- 6. Count the distinct StudyInstanceUIDs that have ANY of the three series types above (union).
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID") AS "union_ImagingSeries_study_count"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND (
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%' OR
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%' OR
        "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
      );
```

```sql
-- 7. View 20 segmentation rows belonging to the collection
--    (these are SEG objects, not the image series).
SELECT
  "StudyInstanceUID",
  "SeriesInstanceUID",
  "segmented_SeriesInstanceUID",
  "SegmentNumber"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS
WHERE "PatientID" ILIKE 'QIN_P%REPEAT%'   -- loose match if PatientID embeds collection name
  OR "StudyInstanceUID" IN (
        SELECT DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID"
        FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
        WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
     )
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count distinct studies whose SEG objects correspond to T2 Weighted Axial image series.
--    Join SEGMENTATIONS to the parent imaging series by SeriesInstanceUID.
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT s."StudyInstanceUID") AS "t2_axial_segmentation_study_count"
FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS  s
JOIN IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT    p
  ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
  AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%';
```

```sql
-- 9. Obtain, side‑by‑side, the counts of studies for all four categories.
SELECT
  (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID")
     FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
     WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
       AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%')                                   AS "cnt_DWI",
  (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID")
     FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
     WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
       AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%')                    AS "cnt_T2_WAxial",
  (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT "StudyInstanceUID")
     FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
     WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
       AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%')       AS "cnt_ADC",
  (SELECT COUNT(DISTINCT s."StudyInstanceUID")
     FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS s
     JOIN IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT   p
       ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
     WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
       AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%')                  AS "cnt_T2_WAxial_SEG";
```

```sql
-- 10. Final single query: distinct StudyInstanceUIDs that have ANY of the
--     four specified categories (DWI, T2WAxial image, ADC, T2WAxial SEG).
SELECT
  COUNT(DISTINCT uid) AS "all_fourCategories_union_study_count"
FROM (
  /* Image series: DWI */
  SELECT "StudyInstanceUID" AS uid
  FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
  WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
    AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%DWI%'
  UNION
  /* Image series: T2 Weighted Axial */
  SELECT "StudyInstanceUID" AS uid
  FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
  WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
    AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
  UNION
  /* Image series: Apparent Diffusion Coefficient */
  SELECT "StudyInstanceUID" AS uid
  FROM IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT
  WHERE "collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
    AND "SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%Apparent%Diffusion%Coefficient%'
  UNION
  /* Segmentations derived from T2 Weighted Axial image series */
  SELECT s."StudyInstanceUID" AS uid
  FROM IDC.IDC_V17.SEGMENTATIONS s
  JOIN IDC.IDC_V17.DICOM_PIVOT p
    ON p."SeriesInstanceUID" = s."segmented_SeriesInstanceUID"
  WHERE p."collection_id" = 'qin_prostate_repeatability'
    AND p."SeriesDescription" ILIKE '%T2%Weighted%Axial%'
) AS u;
```

